<title>BELGIUM: EU invites durum wheat importers to reclaim duty.</title>
<headline>EU invites durum wheat importers to reclaim duty.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European grain importers who shipped in durum wheat between January and June this year have 14 days to claim back duty owing to them, the EU Official Journal said.</p>
<p>Under EU regulation 2228/96, traders can claim back duty on imports of up to 25,000 tonnes in the first half of 1996 and up to 50,000 tonnes for imports between July 1 and November 25.</p>
<p>The notice inviting applications for reimbursement was published in EU Official Journal C 351/8.</p>
<p>The special GATT duty-free quota arrangement follows the enlargement of the European Union to include Austria, Finland and Sweden.</p>
<p>- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
